IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tma-types`

-- Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK) — GOAL 1: RETURNS (ss 7, 8, 9ZA, 9A).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1970-9.txt.

§ `Goal 1 — returns`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- s 7(1C)(a): "the period of 6 months from the end of the year of
-- assessment" — the year ends on 5 April Y+1, so the period ends 5 October.
@ref s 7(1), (1A), (1C)(a)
@export The last day to notify HMRC of chargeability to income tax or capital gains tax under s 7 of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK) for a person not given a notice to file: 6 months from the end of the year of assessment, 5 October after the tax year. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`  @desc The tax year
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify chargeability for` r MEANS
    Date 5 10 (r's `tax year` PLUS 1)

-- s 8(1D) "(a) in the case of a non-electronic return, on or before 31st
-- October in Year 2, and (b) in the case of an electronic return, on or
-- before 31st January in Year 2." (1F) Exception 1: notice after 31 July
-- but on or before 31 October in Year 2 — paper within "the period of 3
-- months beginning with the date of the notice", electronic by 31 January.
-- (1G) Exception 2: notice after 31 October in Year 2 — either kind within
-- the 3 months beginning with the notice.
@ref s 8(1D)-(1G)
@export The last day to deliver a self-assessment return under s 8 of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): 31 October after the tax year (paper) or 31 January following (electronic); for a notice given after 31 July but by 31 October, 3 months from the notice (paper) or 31 January (electronic); for a notice after 31 October, 3 months from the notice. NOTHING if no notice was given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`  @desc The tax year, the date of the notice to file, and whether the return is electronic
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the filing deadline for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `notice to file given on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST n THEN
        JUST (BRANCH
                IF n GREATER THAN oct31 THEN `the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` n
                IF n GREATER THAN jul31 THEN
                    IF r's `electronic return` THEN jan31 ELSE `the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` n
                OTHERWISE
                    IF r's `electronic return` THEN jan31 ELSE oct31)
    WHERE
        y MEANS r's `tax year`
        jul31 MEANS Date 31 7 (y PLUS 1)
        oct31 MEANS Date 31 10 (y PLUS 1)
        jan31 MEANS Date 31 1 (y PLUS 2)

-- s 9ZA(3): "the filing date" is 31 January of Year 2, or, if the notice was
-- given after 31 October of Year 2, the last day of the 3 months beginning
-- with the notice. (2) "An amendment may not be made more than twelve months
-- after the filing date."
@ref s 9ZA(2)-(3)
GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the filing date under s 9ZA for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `notice to file given on`
    WHEN JUST n THEN
        IF   n GREATER THAN Date 31 10 (r's `tax year` PLUS 1)
        THEN `the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` n
        ELSE Date 31 1 (r's `tax year` PLUS 2)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 31 1 (r's `tax year` PLUS 2)

@ref s 9ZA(2)
@export The last day for a taxpayer to amend a self-assessment return under s 9ZA of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): twelve months after the filing date (31 January after the tax year, or the end of 3 months from a notice given after 31 October). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`  @desc The tax year and the date of the notice to file
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to amend the return for` r MEANS
    `add months` (`the filing date under s 9ZA for` r) 12

-- s 9A(2) "the quarter days are 31st January, 30th April, 31st July and 31st
-- October": the next one strictly after a day.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the quarter day next following` d MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF d LESS THAN Date 31 1 y THEN Date 31 1 y
        IF d LESS THAN Date 30 4 y THEN Date 30 4 y
        IF d LESS THAN Date 31 7 y THEN Date 31 7 y
        IF d LESS THAN Date 31 10 y THEN Date 31 10 y
        OTHERWISE Date 31 1 (y PLUS 1)
    WHERE
        y MEANS DATE_YEAR d

-- s 9A(2) "(a) if the return was delivered on or before the filing date, up
-- to the end of the period of twelve months after the day on which the
-- return was delivered; (b) if the return was delivered after the filing
-- date, up to and including the quarter day next following the first
-- anniversary of the day on which the return was delivered; (c) if the
-- return is amended under section 9ZA ..., up to and including the quarter
-- day next following the first anniversary of the day on which the amendment
-- was made."
@ref s 9A(2)
@export The last day for HMRC to give notice of enquiry into a self-assessment return under s 9A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): twelve months after delivery for a return delivered by the filing date; for a late return, the quarter day (31 January, 30 April, 31 July, 31 October) next following the first anniversary of delivery; for an amended return, the later of that and the quarter day next following the first anniversary of the amendment. NOTHING if no return was delivered. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Return facts`  @desc The tax year, the notice date, and the dates of delivery and any amendment
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day for a notice of enquiry for` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `delivered on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        JUST (CONSIDER r's `amended on`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN base d
              WHEN JUST a  THEN `the later of` (base d) (`the quarter day next following` (`add months` a 12)))
    WHERE
        GIVEN d IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        -- s 9A(6): here "the filing date" is "the last day for delivering it
        -- in accordance with section 8" (changed after the independent pass,
        -- D5, D6, D14: not the s 9ZA(3) date). With no notice, the s 9ZA date
        -- is used.
        base d MEANS
            IF   d AT MOST filingDate
            THEN `add months` d 12
            ELSE `the quarter day next following` (`add months` d 12)
        filingDate MEANS
            CONSIDER `the filing deadline for` r
            WHEN JUST f  THEN f
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `the filing date under s 9ZA for` r
